# Campaign throughput refinement


## Throughput refinement authorized 2026-09-12

Apply to new dispatches after this refinement; do not rewrite frozen inputs.
Both independent proposal angles use gpt-6-astra/high when available. Preserve
angle independence: shared original sources are allowed, other-angle judgments
and root review targets remain withheld until both drafts freeze. No semantic
stage, canonical generation or required fidelity suite is removed.

Keep reports compact and specific to the segment. Put complete source evidence,
query results and mechanical proof in structured files; reference exact paths
and hashes from prose instead of repeating the same evidence catalog in every
report. Identical original evidence may be stored once per angle/batch with
explicit references. Each source claim must remain independently reproducible;
no missing evidence is excused by the shorter report format. Record source names,
exact quoted fields, query parameters/counts, contentious decisions, omissions,
counts and final hashes. Preserve all failed/superseded attempts.

Root will record actual dispatch and completion timestamps for subsequent stages,
including role/model, selected sequence range and immutable input/output hashes.
Past approximate stage comparisons are observational, not precise benchmarks.

For future semantic evidence collection, use one exact-byte content-addressed
copy for repeated original evidence and preserve a complete original-to-copy
manifest (multiple original paths may map to one identical copy). The individual
final spec/body/report interfaces remain per segment. Reviewers still independently
reopen the originals, verify hashes and examine every proposed correspondence.
Do not retrofit old frozen evidence; do not replace proof with an unverified cache.
Canonical generators, source comparisons and all existing required suites still
execute for each new accepted page. No test-result caching is authorized here.
